{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"8fed70b81f8a3e2d","x":-541,"y":-343,"width":321,"height":63,"type":"text","text":"Device \nenvía mensaje `sync` "},
		{"id":"d391fc29697139f9","type":"text","text":"cl-perte recibe el mensaje","x":-40,"y":-343,"width":321,"height":63},
		{"id":"2ef97b834098ee1c","type":"text","text":"    → driver/translator.perteSyncParser.parse() descompone el array:\n     const [plmn_op, plmn_rev] = plmn;  // plmn_op=1, plmn_rev=3\n     → genera: { plmn: { plmn_op: 1, plmn_rev: 3 } }\n     ↓\n","x":440,"y":-355,"width":362,"height":87},
		{"id":"bcd1b364e7e6ad1a","type":"text","text":"sync.perte → handleInput() recibe el mensaje parseado\n","x":1040,"y":-355,"width":362,"height":87},
		{"id":"0bdc9645e3a14584","type":"text","text":">[!important] campo plmn\n>El campo `plmn` es un **array de 2 números**: `[operator, [[tableRevision]]]`.","x":-63,"y":-208,"width":263,"height":148},
		{"id":"ac5e10b47c71a332","x":-580,"y":-208,"width":400,"height":240,"type":"text","text":"`mensaje`\n\n```js\n{\n  \"id\": [\"23031300000001\", 4812, 23, 1, 5],\n  \"ty\": \"sync\",\n  \"ts\": 1774451808,\n  \"bid\": 1,\n  \"hw\": [\"123456789012345\", \"8934071111111111111\", \"214071234567890\", \"BC95-G\", \"V100R100C10B657SP2\"],\n  \"plmn\": [1, 3],\n  \"d\": [[10, 2, 0, 0], [11, 5, 1, 1]]\n}\n```"},
		{"id":"02003b3a5408006b","x":-599,"y":-920,"width":325,"height":103,"type":"text","text":"Admin en frontend → crea un plmnList con: operator, release, plmnTable (texto MCC-MNC)"},
		{"id":"e0f07bd11ba5d773","type":"text","text":"API publica mensaje en RabbitMQ → topic: \"command.plmn\"","x":-193,"y":-920,"width":325,"height":103},
		{"id":"c2b2d37b89b54ff1","type":"text","text":">[!important] `TableRevision`\n\n**listado de códigos MCC-MNC** (Mobile Country Code + Mobile Network Code) separados por saltos de línea. Mira el ejemplo comentado en el código:\n\n```\n20205    ← KPN (Países Bajos)\n20404    ← Vodafone NL\n21401    ← Vodafone España\n22210    ← Vodafone Italia\n26201    ← Telekom Alemania\n310410   ← AT&T (USA)\n...\n```\n\nSon los operadores de red donde la SIM del device tiene **permiso de roaming**. Cada operador de telecomunicaciones (en este caso Vodafone/GDSP) proporciona esta lista.\n\nCada vez que se genera un nuevo `.bin` con una tabla PLMN actualizada, lleva un `operator` y un `release` (la revisión).\n\nEntonces:\n\n- **`operator`** = identificador del operador (ej: `1` = Vodafone)\n- **`release`** (tableRevision) = versión de esa tabla (ej: `3` = tercera revisión)\n","x":-562,"y":-699,"width":563,"height":240},
		{"id":"26c1e35dd9761327","type":"text","text":". commands/plmn → handleCommandPLMN()\n\n→ Parsea la tabla texto en líneas\n\n→ Genera el binario con CRC16\n\n→ Guarda el .bin en: files/plmn/plmn_op{X}_r{Y}_{timestamp}.bin\n\n→ Actualiza plmnlist en MongoDB: filePath + active=true","x":281,"y":-920,"width":325,"height":103},
		{"id":"42a70017f243f5a8","type":"text","text":"1. Device PERTE envía request GET /{serialNumber}/plmn por CoAP/MQTTS","x":-620,"y":174,"width":325,"height":103},
		{"id":"68f751ed7a209b35","type":"text","text":"2. cl-perte recibe → messageProcessor.process() → retiveAction = \"plmn\"","x":-214,"y":174,"width":325,"height":103},
		{"id":"a9bd4cd04c0f8d54","type":"text","text":">[!warning] Aqui tendre que ahce","x":260,"y":174,"width":325,"height":103}
	],
